Keep horizontal panels within narrow Android viewports.

A fixed 300px panel minimum can exceed the space left beside the activity bar
and side bars. Toggling a side bar then expands the grid beyond the viewport,
and hiding the panel does not necessarily shrink the parent branch again.

Use the same shared width budget as the editor for top and bottom panels.
Clamp exhausted budgets to zero. Desktop and vertical panels retain their
300px minimum; querying editor dimensions for a vertical panel would recurse
through this getter. Panel height and stored sizes are unchanged.

